# Results
# results

# Human study: the ANSWER KEY maps each screen back to its rung and declared answer, so
# committing it next to the annotator forms would put the ground truth one directory away
# from the people being asked to judge blind. The generated screens are large and
# reproducible from `scripts/export_human_study.py --seed`, so none of it is tracked;
# collected `responses_*.jsonl` should be archived deliberately, not by default.
artifacts/human_study/
# The validation study's answer key (which version is which rung, which claim pairs are
# gold relations, which claims are false). Regenerated by
# scripts/build_human_study_release.py; the annotator-facing tasks are in
# docs/human_study_release/, and the key must never sit beside them in the repo.
artifacts/human_study_release/
artifacts/smoke/
data/factuality/
# The evaluation sample: 78 MB of copied contexts, and exactly reproducible from
# its recorded seed via scripts/sample_factuality_corpus.py.
data/factuality_sample/*.jsonl
# LoCoBench generation working state. The released corpus is data/locobench-opus-5-5/,
# merged from these shards by scripts/locobench_shards.py; the shard tree (logs, per-shard
# stores, pre-reset backups, regen scratch dirs) is reproducible intermediate state.
data/locobench-opus-5-5-shards/
data/locobench-opus-5-5-pilot/
data/locobench-opus-5-5.pre-control-fix/
data/locobench-opus-5-5-regen-f063/

# Mined-arm working state for the release. results/locobench_opus_5_5_mined/ commits its
# merged results.json, records/ and by_item/; the per-arm run folders under arms/ are
# duplicates of records/ plus raw logs, and are regenerated by
# scripts/run_locobench_mined_release.sh with --resume.
results/locobench_opus_5_5_mined/arms/
results/locobench_opus_5_5_mined/merge.log
# NLI verdict caches written by scripts/run_ladder_baselines.py --nli-cache-dir.
results/ladder_baselines_release_*/nli_cache/

# LoCoBench dev-set rung repair working state (2026-11). The repaired corpus is
# data/locobench-claude-5-test-v2/, assembled from these per-run stores by
# scripts/merge_locobench_repair.py (provenance in its config.json); each is a full
# `locobench-repair` output and reproducible from its recorded config.
data/locobench-claude-5-test-v2-*/
# Graph-miner per-arm run folders duplicate each arm's records/ plus raw logs, and are
# regenerated by scripts/run_locobench_graph_dev.sh with --resume. The merged arms'
# results and the raw sample cache (samples/) are kept.
results/locobench_claude_5_graph/arms/
# Evaluation of the superseded 8-family old-ladder v2 (data/...-v2-oldladder/).
results/locobench_claude_5_v2_eval/
